196: 2    Formulas for the representations of SL(2, Z).
197: 
198: In this section we analyse a family of unitary representations of SL(2, Z) asso-
199: ciated with a complex finite dimensional simple Lie algebra g. First let us fix
200: some notation for g. (For details about standard material for Lie algebras we
201: refer to [22].) Let h be a Cartan subalgebra of g, and let h∗R be the R–vector
202: space spanned by the roots. We let X and Y be the weight lattice and the root
203: lattice respectively. Let h·, ·i be the standard
204:                                         √        inner product in h∗R normalized
205: such that the long roots have length 2. (That is, h·, ·i is proportional to the
206: inner product induced by the Killing form of g restricted to h.) Then the short
207: 
