235: Let us fix a set Π = {α1 , α2 , . . . , αl } of simple roots in the following and let
236: {λ1 , λ2 , . . . , λl } be the set of fundamental dominant weights relative to Π. The
237: (open) fundamental Weyl chamber (relative to Π) is the set
238:                      FWC = {x ∈ h∗R | hx, αi i > 0, i = 1, . . . , l}.
239: We let C = FWC be the topological closure of FWC. For a positive integer k ,
240: the k –alcove (relative to Π) is the (closed) set
241:                               Ck = {x ∈ C | hx, θi ≤ k},
242: where θ is the highest root of g (relative to Π). (Note that θ is a long root).
243: We will also need the following sets:
244:                  Qk = {c1 λ1 + . . . + cl λl | c1 , . . . , cl ∈ [0, k[ },
