301: Proof The invariance under the action by an element u ∈ W follows by the
302: fact that u is orthogonal together with the identity det(ww′ ) = det(u−1 wu−1 w′ )
303: and the fact that W preserves Y ∨ /aY ∨ (since it preserves Y ∨ ). The invariance
304: under the action by an element kx, x ∈ Y ∨ , is obvious. (For |a| = 1, use (1)
305: and (2).) To prove the last claim, let λ ∈ X ∩ Hα,n k   for a positive root α and
306: an integer n, and let sα be the reflection in α. Fix a w ∈ W and get
